---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import WebhookRetryCalculator from '../../components/WebhookRetryCalculator.jsx';
---
<ToolLayout title="Webhook Retry Strategy Calculator" description="Calculate an exponential backoff retry schedule for delivering webhooks reliably.">
  <WebhookRetryCalculator client:load slot="tool" />

  <h2>Why webhook reliability depends on the sender, not the receiver</h2>
  <p>Unlike a request a client actively waits for, a webhook receiver might be temporarily down when you try to deliver — a good retry schedule (matching patterns used by major providers like Stripe and GitHub) means transient receiver downtime doesn't result in permanently lost events.</p>

  <h2>How to use this calculator</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Set your maximum retry attempts and base delay.</li>
    <li>See the calculated exponential backoff schedule across attempts.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Common Webhook Retry Mistakes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Retrying at a fixed short interval</strong> instead of exponential backoff, hammering a receiver that's already struggling.</li>
    <li><strong>Not setting a maximum retry limit</strong>, retrying indefinitely for a webhook endpoint that will never come back.</li>
    <li><strong>Not providing a way for receivers to replay missed webhooks</strong> after exhausting all automatic retries, leaving no recovery path for extended outages.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When to Use This Webhook Retry Calculator</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Designing a reliable webhook delivery system for your own API</li>
    <li>Understanding how long a webhook provider like Stripe might keep retrying a failed delivery</li>
    <li>Planning receiver-side capacity for handling retry bursts after downtime</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Webhook Retry FAQ</h2>
  <p><strong>How long do major providers typically retry?</strong> This varies by provider, but many retry over a window of hours to a day using exponential backoff before giving up — check your specific provider's documentation for their exact retry policy.</p>
</ToolLayout>
